.4 relationships as a whole to catch the recurring missing-gate family rather than accepting only the two fixture fixes.\nRetain closed findings: canonical Lease Record identity, lagging copies, required parked sources, seven capabilities, live changed-record refusal and previously established predecessor/reducer/enum behavior. Do not repeat unrelated closed audits without new evidence. Shared API caller boundary is accepted; do not shrink remaining assigned requirements.\nCheck final-source provenance and actual exits for new narrowing mutants and same-instrument applied survivor; NOT_APPLIED/compile failure are not behavioral kills. Corrected formatting evidence must use existing paths. Reuse trustworthy exact-source prior evidence with explicit bounds; run necessary new independent regressions. All CI is local. Never edit the active product candidate or integrate; attach task-scoped verdict and raw evidence, then route accept_cr or changes requested through the normal lifecycle.\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev6.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev6.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2183`\n- Content digest: `sha256:f366940896a06c99b9d895b6cc9df27d63619f290c91fdc65471b7b79a4d0449`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-after-rev6.md\nIndependently review the newly published candidate after CR6. Read CR6 verdict/evidence, producer outcome and required clause-to-owner conformance matrix. Verify checkpoint persistence against actual Session.kind for winner and necessary ancestry with positive direct/task_board and wrong-variant controls through BuildPlan, old-plan Revalidate and both summaries. Verify N-chain-self compiles and reaches its intended admission violation on exact final source; inspect affected shipped plants plus applied harmless survivor with real exit evidence.\nThe repeated authority family requires checking the matrix against actual APIs and pinned5.3/5.4/14.7.2, distinguishing canonical shape, related-record semantics and accepted caller/publication responsibilities. Do not accept claimed delegation if the owner lacks required input. Retain closed ancestry/creator, canonical identity, lagging copies, parked source, capabilities and earlier predecessor/reducer/crash findings unless new evidence contradicts them. No scope reduction or demand to implement caller-owned publication/storage/transport. Preserve8-row AC denominator and precise evidence limits.\nReview immutable current CR bytes, preserve active product/index/branch, all CI local. Attach exact verdict and reproducible evidence before accept_cr or changes-requested routing. No integration or manual commits. Avoid counting compile failures, unapplied plants or empty test selections as behavioral proof.\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev7.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev7.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2413`\n- Content digest: `sha256:ead21b996e9f2fd7285d4188eb4acaa8b1f6a04d8eec572e29db501a00573060`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-after-rev7.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-after-rev7.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2280`\n- Content digest: `sha256:c1f0c38b9da1af222d2c643347352f1d3d0fc97900b3dc482508c4c2f195279c`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev8.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev8.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2860`\n- Content digest: `sha256:616f7e582e4568edaaf5ebfa0d3d56cc3f30af5089f973e04beeedc5da81fc13`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-after-rev8.md\nSuperseded on 2026-09-16 by TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-cr9.md (Astra low policy). The original text is retained at .te